  "body": "## Associated User Story\nAs a manager, I want to promote other members or officers to manager, so that leadership of the org can be shared and handed off without needing a developer or database change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n### Managers sit above officers and can promote others to manager.\n\n- Sunny: A logged-in manager opens the member list or a member’s record and selects “Promote to Manager.” The system asks for confirmation, then updates that person’s role and shows a success message. The new manager immediately gets manager access, including everything officers can already do (such as uploading events and attendance and viewing any member’s points and active status) plus the ability to promote others. The promotion is logged with who made the change, who was promoted, and when.\n\n- Rainy: An officer or regular member tries to promote someone, or opens the promote option directly, and is blocked with a clear message that only managers can do this. If the promotion fails (the member can’t be found, the person is already a manager, or the update errors out), the manager sees a clear “try again later or contact a manager” message instead of a blank page or a silently unchanged role, and no one ends up with the wrong role.\n\n\n\nDefinition of Done -\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied: \n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented; \n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes); \n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.\n\n## Evidence \n### Tests pass\n<img width=\"787\" height=\"345\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-10-28 132943\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1ffd882b-b725-4b17-a296-1a301d53e1b5\" />\n\n### Rubocop\n<img width=\"1252\" height=\"347\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-10-28 133127\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e7d28509-3d73-4e69-a8bc-feb7fef5cbc6\" />\n\n",
